;;; theorem-library/riesz-markov-cantor.scm -- RIESZ-MARKOV, STAGE 2 (RM-2,
;;; 2026-10-10): a positive linear functional on the continuous functions of the
;;; Cantor model K is integration against a measure.  Vocabulary:
;;; structure-library/positive-functional.scm (CONT-FNS, IS-POSITIVE-FUNCTIONAL,
;;; CLOPEN-SETS) and structure-library/riesz-markov-model.scm (K, cylinders).
;;; Source: the user's notes-63, form (b).  Helper prefix: rmc-.
;;; 69 theorems, every one `proven modulo 0' (oracles arith, ineq, crs); no support,
;;; warrant, stamp or add-axiom!.
;;;
;;; THE HEADLINES.  For a metric space s and a positive functional lam on CONT-FNS(s):
;;;   rmc-cont-fns-add / -scale  CONT-FNS(s) is closed under pointwise sum and scalar multiple (MOVED 2026-10-20 to cont-fns-laws.scm, same names).
;;;   rmc-indicator-cont         (item 1) the indicator of a clopen set is continuous;
;;;   rmc-cyl-indicator-cont     in particular that of a cylinder of K = RM-KMS(s, dseq).
;;;   rmc-clopen-algebra         (item 2) CLOPEN-SETS(s) is an algebra of sets on PTS s;
;;;   rmc-ind-additive           u |-> lam(1_u) is finitely additive (rmc-ind-nonneg: >= 0).
;;;   compact-closed-countable-subcover (MOVED to metric-finite-subcover.scm, 2026-10-20): a closed set of a compact space covered by open csq(n),
;;;                              n in NN, is covered by those with n below some bound.
;;;   rmc-countable-subadditive  (item 3) on a compact s, a clopen set covered by a sequence
;;;                              of clopen sets has content <= the ESUM of theirs;
;;;   rmc-premeasure             the content is an IS-PREMEASURE on CLOPEN-SETS(s).
;;;   rmc-outer-on-clopen        (item 4) the method-I outer measure OUT of the content
;;;                              agrees with it on clopen sets (s compact);
;;;   rmc-clopen-measurable      clopen sets are Caratheodory-measurable for OUT;
;;;   rmc-measure                MU = RES(OUT, SIG), SIG = CARATHEODORY-SETS(PTS s, OUT), is a
;;;                              measure, SIG contains the clopen sets, MU(u) = lam(1_u) there;
;;;   rmc-k-measure              on K moreover SIG contains every Borel set (an open set of K
;;;                              is the countable union of the clopen sets W(ou, nb) of the
;;;                              points whose cylinder of length nb lies in it).
;;;   rmc-riesz-markov-k         (item 5) for g in CONT-FNS(K): g is IS-INTEGRABLE for MU and
;;;                              RINTEGRAL(g) = lam(g).
;;; ROUTE OF ITEM 5.  g is bounded (rmc-cont-bounded, by the finite subcover) and has open,
;;; hence measurable, tails, so it is integrable (rmc-bounded-integrable, |g| <= B 1).  The
;;; "good" functions (continuous, integrable, integral = lam-value) contain the clopen
;;; indicators and are closed under sums and scalar multiples (rmc-good-ind / -add / -scale).
;;; A continuous g varies by <= eps on the cylinders of one level N (rmc-uniform-level);
;;; f = g o r, r(x) = CHOICE of the cylinder of x of level N, is constant on those
;;; cylinders, within eps of g, and in [-B, B]; THE LAYER INDUCTION (rmc-layer) approximates
;;; any such f within eps by a good function, peeling the top layer {f > c + n eps} (a
;;; saturated, hence clopen, set) one eps at a time -- no finite sum over cylinders is ever
;;; formed.  Both lam and RINTEGRAL are monotone, so |RINTEGRAL g - lam g| <= 4 eps lam(1);
;;; rr-le-all-pos-nonpos closes.
;;;
;;; LOAD WINDOW: [after theorem-library/metric-outer-measure, end).  The latest citations:
;;; borel-sets-unfold, esum-nn-superadditive (metric-outer-measure), the rintegral- laws
;;; (real-integral), outer-measure-construction, caratheodory; RM-1's file
;;; (riesz-markov-model) loads earlier.  Vocabulary: structure-library/positive-functional
;;; (analysis), anywhere after metric-continuity; put it immediately before this file.
;;; Library of this file: measure.  No top-level macro: the file may be compiled.

